# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Local virtualenv created by run.sh on Linux/macOS
.venv/

# PyInstaller / build outputs
build/
dist/
# C++ ASan-instrumented build tree used to hunt the save-path use-after-free
build-asan/
# AppImage build artifacts (belong in dist/; ignore stray ones too)
*.AppImage
*.AppImage.zsync
# Compiled installer -- published as a GitHub Release asset, not committed
installer/

# Local editor / tool settings
.claude/

# Local reference screenshots (not part of the app)
MD_Note.jpg

# Personal working note, kept in the repo folder for convenience only.  This
# repo is PUBLIC: tn.md holds a real tech-note title and organisational
# identifiers, so it must never be committed.  Ignored by name rather than
# left untracked because release.ps1 refuses to run on a dirty tree, and the
# obvious way out of that is a `git add -A` that would publish it.
tn.md

# Credential material, for the same reason and more urgently: a password sheet
# was found sitting untracked in this folder on 2026-08-16, one `git add -A`
# from being published to a PUBLIC repo.  Ignored by name AND by pattern,
# because the next one will not be called the same thing.  Keeping such a file
# outside the repo entirely is better than relying on this.
1 - Password Sheet.pdf
*Password*.pdf
*Password*.md
*password*.csv
logins.md

# Intermediate icon renders (source is mdboss.svg; runtime uses mdboss.ico)
mdboss_*.png

# C++ port: failure dumps written beside the golden corpus by the parity
# tests.  The goldens themselves ARE tracked -- they are the expectation.
MDBossCpp/tests/golden/*.actual.*

# Third-party vendored assets are tracked (assets/); nothing here is ignored.
